Scope clarification, 31 October 2026

The MIT licence above covers original Treasury code and technical documentation,
including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, scripts and tests. Creative content embedded in
code or HTML is subject to its own terms; embedding does not change those terms.

For new original Treasury artwork, illustrations and other creative assets,
unless separately licensed: to the extent Sam holds the necessary rights, you
may use, copy, modify and share them to run and develop The Treasury, including
modified versions of The Treasury. No permission is granted under these terms
to reuse them in unrelated products, asset packs or branding. Other rights are
reserved. This does not assert exclusive rights in AI-generated material or
grant rights that Sam does not hold.

Existing grants remain valid. This clarification does not withdraw or restrict
permissions already granted for distributed versions or assets. In particular,
the chest and icon bytes identified in ARTWORK.md were already distributed
under the earlier broad MIT licence; those MIT permissions remain available
for those bytes and copies of them, including in later Treasury versions.

Third-party assets and marks retain their own terms, as listed in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. The MIT licence and creative-asset terms do not grant
trademark rights. No licence to anyone's personal financial records is granted;
they are not part of this source package.
